WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:14.080
Have you ever heard of dragonflies that snipe
their prey with bolts of energy?

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.150
Or octopuses that serve as guard dogs?

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.759
Or Necromancer Bees that live in reanimated
carcass-hives?

00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:25.849
These images aren’t pulled from some bizarre
medieval manuscript.

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:29.320
Nor are they long-lost Renaissance paintings.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.400
These are from the Codex Inversus — a modern
worldbuilding project from the imagination

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.010
of the brilliant artist and writer Luca Vanzella.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:43.329
Brought to life through collages of classical
art, the world of Codex Inversus is full of

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:49.540
flora and fauna that have evolved to use magical
energy, visitors from parallel dimensions,

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.430
and fractures in space and time.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:56.940
At a glance, the surreal, scrambled visuals
are difficult to make sense of.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:03.030
Yet like a medieval bestiary, the project
does follow a unique system of internal logic.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:09.000
So, for this entry into the archive, I’ll
investigate the creatures, people, and locations

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:18.060
of this scrambled world — and reveal the
hidden order to the chaos of Codex Inversus…

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:23.561
The land of Codex Inversus exists in the wake
of a cosmic upheaval known as the Collapse

00:01:23.561 --> 00:01:29.340
— where all extradimensional realms crashed
into the material world, releasing vast magical

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.640
energies that altered reality.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.329
Understanding the realm as it exists today
is no easy task, for the world is full of

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.280
strange oddities.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.369
Yet we must start somewhere.

00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:46.270
In the center of the northernmost continent
lies the Valley of Delights, a relatively

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.930
safe and idyllic region where magic practitioners
create surreal sights.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:54.219
But it’s not just people casting the magic.

00:01:54.219 --> 00:02:00.590
In Codex Inversus, even small creatures — like
the bizarre Transmuter Snail — have evolved

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.880
to use simple spells.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.509
In their neutral form, a Transmuting Snail
is indistinguishable from an ordinary snail.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:15.310
Yet if, say, a plant is out of reach, a Transmuter
Snail will move their eye stalks in specific

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.449
patterns to rapidly change their body, gaining
frog-like legs for jumping.

00:02:20.449 --> 00:02:25.630
If trying to cross a puddle, a Transmuter
Snail might adopt a ‘swimming form,’ gaining

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.919
a tail similar to a tadpole’s.

00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:33.639
And when trying to carry an object, these
snails might even gain a long prehensile appendage

00:02:33.639 --> 00:02:37.709
— equivalent to an octopus tentacle...

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:43.940
The first human spellcasters, called the Evokers,
learned how to wield magic by studying animals

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.270
like the Transmuter Snail.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:51.540
These early wizards found that existence can
be shifted with the right pattern… and that

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.840
pulling on the threads of reality can be dangerous.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:01.280
For spells in Codex Inversus are strange and
unpredictable, often altering the user’s

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.630
physical body beyond recognition.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:10.000
And in the Valley of Delight, some spellcasters
have also begun altering the biology of animals.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.820
The Chimericat is the result of artificial
speciation through transmutation magic.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:21.040
With a spring-like body and piercing tail,
Chimericats are designed to be the ultimate

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.380
form of pest control.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:28.530
For while the valley is an idyllic locale,
it has a bit of a rat problem.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:33.660
Manticorats are winged rodents that never
evolved to cast spells themselves, but are

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.500
quite adept at sniffing out magical ingredients
on which to feed.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:42.720
And while the Chimericats proved effective
at catching the Manticorats, now the valley

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.780
is overrun with Chimericats instead…

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:53.880
In Codex Inversus, human attempts to rewrite
existence often end with disaster.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:59.170
Yet following the collapse of other realms
into the material world, humans now share

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:03.500
territory with wiser, formerly mythic beings.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:08.729
North of the Valley of Delights, the long-lived
Elves build their eternal kingdoms.

00:04:08.729 --> 00:04:14.280
Elves possess a greater understanding of how
to safely cast spells than humans, and specialize

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.579
in controlling the elements.

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:21.570
In the mountains of the south, subterranean
Dwarves are more practical in their reality

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:26.760
manipulation, creating artificial beings to
aid in their mining.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.660
And there’s another tunneling lifeform native
to the southern continent.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.650
Abjuring Termites are capable of incredible
feats of engineering.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:40.140
They have evolved to cast spells — not with
their bodies, but with the shape of their

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.140
tunnels.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:46.660
Through the digging of complex patterns, Abjuring
Termite nests are protected by a low-level

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.870
spell, and are virtually indestructible.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:55.410
Termite farms have become novelty items, with
some individuals putting them on display and

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.040
asking guests to try and smash them.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.140
Which is physically impossible.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:02.630
Yet the termites still have predators.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:08.110
The Mudpecker is a bird that uses stealth
to catch termites: inserting their thin beaks

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:13.590
in the nest's pores without causing immediate
alarm and slurping clean one or two tunnels

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.500
before the defenses are alerted.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:21.390
It’s a strategy similar to ordinary woodpeckers,
and suggests that sometimes the best path

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:25.030
is the one of least resistance…

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:31.190
In the southernmost region of the world, perhaps
the strangest lifeforms of all are the Matras.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:37.000
Sentient constructs of unknown origin, these
clockwork beings strive to replace chaotic

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.730
biological life with precise and reliable
artificial creatures.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:48.200
Most notably, the Matras oversee the Enigma
Library, a collection of texts no one is able

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.400
to translate.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:55.500
The artificial, cube-headed Curators of this
library search for a ‘Grand Diagram’ — a

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.460
complete and comprehensive explanation of
how the Collapse warped creation.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:04.120
So far, they have found nothing...

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:09.480
The primordial chaos of the Collapse has changed
some populations in incredible ways.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:14.030
The seafaring Halflings possess bodies that
defy perspective.

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:20.320
Like living optical illusions, they seem to
have pieces missing from certain angles.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:25.960
These unsettling gaps, which are common on
hands and arms, cause no pain, and are the

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:30.960
result of parts of their bodies phasing through
dimensional reality.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:36.860
And as is often the case in Codex Inversus,
certain animals have evolved to take advantage

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.389
of similar magical phenomena.

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:43.530
Conjuring ants are tiny insects with an impressive
secret.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:49.330
Like ordinary ants, Conjuring Ant society
is mainly preoccupied with transporting food

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.740
back to the nest for later consumption.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:57.170
But Conjuring Ants have found a faster method
than carrying food themselves.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:07:03.500
By moving in a specific pattern around a piece
of vegetation, Conjuring Ants can fold spacetime

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:08.580
and teleport food directly back to the nest…

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.220
To the north, reality becomes even further
warped.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:16.780
Here, a marine paradise coexists with a prairie.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:22.210
Known as the Ethereal Ocean, this environment
is possible due to out-of-phase water in the

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:25.250
sky that various fish swim through.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:30.580
All animals here can interact with each other
even if they respond to different environmental

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:31.860
conditions.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:37.840
Small fishes graze the fur of horses, sharks
hunt flocks of birds, and spiders weave webs

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.450
to catch flying shrimp.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:45.760
In this vast region where the sky behaves
like the sea, certain groups of wizards have

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:51.230
domesticated octopuses — which fill a role
similar to dogs or cats.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:56.581
Some breeds of octopuses are able to hunt
for vermin and scare off intruders, while

00:07:56.581 --> 00:08:01.340
others are clever enough to fetch tools and
alchemical ingredients.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:07.290
Some Magi Octopuses can even cast small spells
— although they are too shy to do so in

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.040
public…

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:14.010
The Ethereal Ocean is part of a kingdom called
the Angelic Unison.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:19.440
Ruled by the ethereal descendants of celestial
beings, the land is a place where anything

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.639
can happen.

00:08:20.639 --> 00:08:27.160
A realm of infinite wonders, at the heart
of the Angelic Unison are grassy plains populated

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.260
by cosmic animals.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:35.500
Stargazing Cows are inherently magical creatures
that produce milk with calming and relaxing

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.500
properties.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:42.020
The restless Insomniac Sheep are the cows’
opposite, with their milk acting as a natural

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:47.870
stimulant — making sheep’s butter a popular
breakfast food across the kingdom.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:53.690
Yet the most important animals in the Angelic
Unison are the Holy Cows.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:58.080
Descendants of extradimensional animals from
before the Collapse that interbred with their

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:03.520
earthly counterparts, Holy Cows possess the
ability to quell aggression just by looking

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.670
at someone.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:10.260
Their halo-horn signifies their importance,
and their milk always tastes sweet, even when

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:16.460
spoiled — which can actually be problematic,
and can cause sickness if one isn’t careful.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:22.450
The Angelic Unison is a kingdom where almost
all things possess some level of extradimensional

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:23.900
distortion.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:29.440
Even stones take on fantastical properties
in the Floating Plains —a region famed for

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.010
its slabs of levitating rock.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:37.560
While an interesting novelty, these boulders
can also be something of a nuisance — disrupting

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:42.610
herds and keeping rain from watering crops.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:48.060
On the western edge of the continent, the
independent Nation of Beasts has formed.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:53.210
Here, many groups of humanoids with animal
features gather together under one banner,

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:56.150
and cast unique spells.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:10:01.370
In crowded cities, the Cat-Folk are a common
sight, filling the nights with the sounds

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.050
of their serenades.

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:08.839
Unfortunately for the general populace, to
be a good singer, or just in tune, is not

00:10:08.839 --> 00:10:10.580
a prerequisite.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.720
Cat-Folk are also excellent weavers and spellcasters.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:19.480
Animal-folk in general have a unique attitude
towards magic, seeing the energies of the

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:25.200
dimensional field as conscious, and spells
a way of "asking" the field for assistance,

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.550
rather than controlling it.

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:32.420
Snake-Folk are another common resident in
cities, preferring to stay indoors due to

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:34.800
their cold-blooded physiology.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:40.339
Their ancestral fangs make chewing difficult,
and so they have a unique culinary tradition

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:42.670
based around soft foods.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:48.920
Snake-Folk cuisine has become famous across
the continent, and many serpents now run popular

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:50.100
taverns.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:55.110
Shambling in the back alleys of the beasts’
cities are unnerving pests.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:01.050
The bodies of deceased animals have been spotted
moving seemingly of their own accord, surrounded

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.170
by buzzing insects.

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:09.170
These corpses are, in fact, the mobile hives
of Necromancer Bees.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:14.600
These bizarre insects have come up with an
ingenious way of scaring off predators — by

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:19.250
hijacking the expired bodies of animals larger
than they are.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:26.190
Necromancer Bees reanimate animals using rather
complicated spells for such tiny insects — moving

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:31.020
in different formations called ‘dances’
to get the muscles of their hives working

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.720
once more.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:38.140
Strange as this might sound, ordinary bees
can actually perform complicated dances to

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:44.700
communicate the direction and distance of
flowers to their fellow hive members…

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:50.070
Deeper within the Nation of Beasts is a bleak
landscape dominated by cubes of rock that

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:52.950
look like they fell from the skies.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:58.910
Known as the Hades Badlands, the region is
a land of oblivion, where reality unravels

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:01.480
due to the cubes’ strange properties.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:08.090
Those who pass through may lose their memory,
their minds, or their physical form.

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:14.600
Even deeper within the Beast Nation, the secretive
Raven-Folk keep watch over the Ghost Forest.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:19.430
While they interact and trade with the other
nations, they do not permit anyone to enter

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.790
their mysterious domain.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:27.990
For while the Ghost Forest might appear like
an ordinary grove, the fog works as a pocket

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:33.110
dimension, which some plants and animals have
evolved to ‘phase’ in and out of.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:37.900
One such plant is the Starberry, which produces
an enticing fruit.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:42.720
It wants to be eaten, but not by ‘ghost
animals,’ since they can ‘phase out’

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:44.730
the seeds during digestion.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:50.241
To prevent this, the fruit possesses a cage
of thorns that stings only ‘ghosts’ — with

00:12:50.241 --> 00:12:53.540
mortals able to pass through it unharmed.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:59.230
Eating a Starberry means putting the bramble
into your mouth, which can be unsettling even

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:01.210
if you know it won't sting.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:07.290
The haunting Ghost Lilies are perhaps the
most important plants of the Ghost Forest.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:13.670
These mind-altering flowers evokes memories
and a sense of nostalgia when smelled or ingested.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:19.200
This property has made the lilies a luxury
good, and a common export to more distant

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.530
parts of the realm…

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:28.510
In the margins of the Codex Inversus world,
one of the rarer and more destructive creatures

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:31.090
are the Evoker Dragonflies.

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:36.279
These insects are carnivorous, and they hunt
like sharpshooters: waiting for their prey

00:13:36.279 --> 00:13:41.730
and then striking from afar with impressive
spells summoned from their tails.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:48.350
To resist the recoil of the bolt, evoker Dragonflies
must use their claws to grab whatever they

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.980
are standing on.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:56.580
The kickback of their dart is also used proactively
as propulsion by the dragonflies, with the

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:01.500
insect shooting a bolt in the opposite direction
they are headed — propelling them at high

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.390
speeds towards their destination.

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:08.720
And destructive magic isn’t limited to insects.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:14.399
Ancient scriptures say that beings known as
the Fairies once wandered the world, spreading

00:14:14.399 --> 00:14:18.500
ruin for no reason other than their own amusement.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:23.860
The even grimmer counterparts of the Fairies
— the Nightmares — also tormented the

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:27.950
land, and drew the ire of the Angelic Unison.

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:33.279
The angelic beings used the last spark of
their divinity to banish them to the two moons

00:14:33.279 --> 00:14:39.000
that orbit the planet, since other dimensions
no longer existed after the collapse.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:44.040
The Nightmares were sent to the Onyx moon,
where scripture says they remain to this day

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:48.760
— ravenous and waiting for a chance to take
their revenge.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:54.450
The fairies were banished to the Jade moon,
and faded into myth over the passing centuries.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:15:00.220
Yet recently, sightings of eerie creatures
wearing domes of jade on their heads have

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:07.360
begun, and strange lights appear in the sky
when the moons are full…

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:13.660
Across the world of Codex Inversus, perhaps
no location is as fabled or as feared as the

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:14.860
Elsewhere Woods.

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:20.990
A piece of crumbled space where reality folds
like paper, the Elsewhere Woods are a place

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:23.080
where lost things go.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:29.680
Some say towers of slithering flesh with geometric
summits rise among the trees, their origin

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:32.110
and function unknown.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:37.279
Others claim the woods are made of many different
trees from all over the world — with patches

00:15:37.279 --> 00:15:44.330
of pine forest and stripes of tropical jungles,
brambles from arid lands fading into wet fields

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.800
of reeds.

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:52.210
Floating among these branches are white Cloud-Possums
— inquisitive marsupials that hover as if

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:54.390
they weigh nothing at all.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:16:00.720
Some reports claim fearsome Owl-Griffins prowl
the Elsewhere Woods, defending their territory

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.910
with fierce attentiveness.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:08.720
What truth there is in such fables is difficult
to say, for few return from the Elsewhere

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:11.620
Woods with their lives.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:17.790
One of the few well-documented beings of the
Elsewhere Woods is the Illusionist Butterfly.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:24.160
Also spotted in other parts of the world,
these insects have an impressive form of camouflage.

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:29.450
From their caterpillar stage, Illusionist
Butterflies are able to change color to match

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:33.320
their surrounding environment with uncanny
precision.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:37.700
Following metamorphosis, however, they hide
in a different way.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:43.760
The venations of their wings form a pattern
capable of casting an illusion spell.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:48.339
Many real butterflies have spots on their
wings that essentially serve the same purpose

00:16:48.339 --> 00:16:52.960
— mimicking the eyes of predators to scare
off would-be attackers.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:58.010
Yet the Illusionist Butterfly takes this a
step further, with their patterns capable

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:03.589
of creating an illusory owl that moves and
flies next to its creator.

00:17:03.589 --> 00:17:08.649
These owl projections are rarely complete,
with their bodies appearing and disappearing

00:17:08.649 --> 00:17:10.069
in a waving shape.

00:17:10.069 --> 00:17:16.269
Still, it’s an incredible form of camouflage
— that shows when in the Elsewhere Woods,

00:17:16.269 --> 00:17:19.850
things are seldom what they appear.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:25.089
Entering the Elsewhere Woods is no easy task,
for the region cannot be accessed through

00:17:25.089 --> 00:17:26.089
mortal means.

00:17:26.089 --> 00:17:31.929
There are rumors that the skulls of cyclops
— giant beings who went extinct long ago

00:17:31.929 --> 00:17:36.330
— act as natural portals into the Elsewhere
Woods.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:42.169
Monsters of unknown origin stalk the caverns
where these skulls can be found — chimeras

00:17:42.169 --> 00:17:45.119
made from many different beings.

00:17:45.119 --> 00:17:50.859
Reports describe creatures with tentacles
arms, necks which split into fanged mouths,

00:17:50.859 --> 00:17:54.090
and disturbing heads shaped like crying children.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:57.379
Yet where could such nightmares have come
from?

00:17:57.379 --> 00:18:03.669
Some have theorized that the cyclops skulls
connect to other places with spatial anomalies.

00:18:03.669 --> 00:18:09.750
There are rumors of a land beyond the ocean,
far from any known landmass, lit by a fracture

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.859
in space known as The Second Horizon.

00:18:12.859 --> 00:18:18.869
No one from the known world has reached the
shores of this land, although many have tried.

00:18:18.869 --> 00:18:24.299
According to legend, the land is populated
with three-eyed people — a lineage different

00:18:24.299 --> 00:18:25.590
from any other.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:30.859
Their land is also populated with Hammergulls
— seagulls with the heads of hammerhead

00:18:30.859 --> 00:18:31.989
sharks.

00:18:31.989 --> 00:18:35.090
What truth is there to such strange tales?

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.859
No one can say for certain.

00:18:36.859 --> 00:18:44.869
For in the margins of Codex Inversus, there
will always be things which evade all understanding...

00:18:44.869 --> 00:18:50.960
Observing the world of Codex Inversus is like
looking through a fractured window, with the

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.389
images shifting and merging before your eyes.

00:18:54.389 --> 00:18:59.789
Yet this scrambled world of fables and myth
follows its own kind of rules if one looks

00:18:59.789 --> 00:19:00.960
closely enough.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:06.640
There are countless other strange and wondrous
aspects of Codex Inversus I wasn’t able

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:12.029
to cover here, and you can see more of the
art and read more of the narrative using the

00:19:12.029 --> 00:19:13.509
links in the description.

00:19:13.509 --> 00:19:18.950
And if you find this world as interesting
as I do, I encourage you to follow and support

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:23.840
Luca Vanzella, who is continuing to flesh
out this dreamlike realm.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:26.710
Once again, links are down below.

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:31.160
And as always, thanks for watching.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:36.139
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
support by liking, subscribing, and hitting

00:19:36.139 --> 00:19:40.820
the notification icon to stay up to date on
all things Curious.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:58.389
See you in the next video.

